# rgedc-phone: the RG Rotate's link to a phone over Bluetooth LE.
#
#  * iPhone: we advertise as "RG EDC" and ask for the Apple Notification Center
#    Service (ANCS). The phone connects from Settings > Bluetooth and pairs, and we
#    read its notifications as a GATT client. Current Time Service sets the clock.
#  * Android: we serve the Nordic UART service and speak the Bangle.js protocol
#    of the Gadgetbridge app (notifications, dismiss, calls, music, time). While
#    "pair Android" mode is on we advertise as "Espruino RG EDC" so Gadgetbridge
#    lists us as a supported device.
#
# The RG EDC shell talks to us over a Unix socket with one JSON object per line
# (see Hub below). Runs from rgedc-phone.service next to bluetoothd; the code is
# plain Python so it can be swapped on the device (/storage/.config/rgedc/rgedc-phone
# wins over this file, see the service).

